## Error Handling

| Situation | Action |
|---|---|
| MCP tool returns error | Retry once; if persistent, stop launching new tasks, wait for already launched tasks to complete, then call `finalize_run(run_id, stop_reason="mcp_error")` |
| evotrias-task-executor fails | Still call `check_convergence`; MCP decides whether to stop or continue from recorded attempts |
| evotrias-meta-guidance-generator returns `not_committed`, fails to return its compact result, or fails generation | Keep the MCP request pending, continue replenishment, and allow one later completion event to retry it |
| evotrias-meta-guidance-generator returns `mcp_error` after its own retry and the authoritative post-check does not confirm a commit | Apply the persistent MCP error rule above |
| User interrupts | Stop launching new tasks; if possible, wait for launched tasks to complete; then call `finalize_run(run_id, stop_reason="user_interrupted")` |
